Q: How do I start chanting?
Sources: Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) | Heart Dharma Intro (EN) · types: introduction,xiaofangzi_guide,qa_metaphysics,qa_general,canonical_ruling
  ✓ names at least one sutra/mantra
  ✓ gives a count (N times / × N / N遍)
  ✓ AND asks the triage question in the same reply
  ✓ no generic 「I dedicate all merits」 closing
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Welcome 🙏 So glad you're here.

Before I give you the full guide, let me ask: **Have you chanted before, or is this completely new to you?**

In the meantime, here's a simple starting point you can use right away:

---

📿 **《千手千眼无碍大悲心陀罗尼》(Great Compassion Mantra)** — 3 times daily
Before chanting, say: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me good health and strengthen my spiritual power."*

📿 **《般若波罗蜜多心经》(Heart Sutra)** — 3 times daily
Before chanting, say: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], grant me wisdom, a clear and calm mind, and remove my worries."*
⚠️ Do not chant after 10pm

📿 **《礼佛大忏悔文》(Eighty-Eight Buddhas Great Repentance)** — 1 time daily
Before chanting, say: *"May the Great Merciful and Great Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva protect and bless me, [your full name], help me repent and eliminate my karmic obstacles."*
⚠️ Do not chant between 10pm–5am

---

Don't worry if you don't know the words yet — there are follow-along videos here:
🔗 https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

Just follow along. Consistency matters more than quantity 🙏

**Have you chanted before?** Your answer helps me suggest the best next steps for you.

